Elon musk's ownership of Twitter has  gotten off to a shaky start in his  latest controversial move he's banned  more than a half dozen Twitter accounts  mainly high-profile Tech journalists who  were reporting on musk's ownership of  the company some like Aaron rupper had  been critical of musk there does seem to  be a goal here to kind of put a chill on  negative coverage of him critical  coverage of him by sort of conveying to  journalists hey you know if you cross me  I can kind of take this all away from  you I can sort of banish you from this  platform that people in the media rely  on the ban had also extended to others  who hadn't been particularly critical of  musk I had a message which popped popped  up which said I was suspended then a  little bit later there was a banner that  came up that said I had been permanently  suspended and if I wanted to appeal it  to click on a particular link I clicked  on that link and it's a broken link late  Thursday musk briefly joined Twitter  spaces chat where he justified  suspending the journalists because he  claimed they doxed him meaning they made  public his live location or personal  information details  musk claims he wants to bring back free  speech to Twitter but Banning these  journalists seems to run counter to that  and up until now most of the talk has  been about the people that musk has  invited back on the platform many of  whom very controversial figures  like this far right troll account used  to make anti-semitic statements it was  suspended in 2007 for violating  Twitter's policy on hateful conduct but  musk reinstated it last week do I think  that it's going to necessarily make musk  Hemorrhage users at this point maybe not  is it incredibly damaging towards the  idea that somehow this is a free speech  absolutist we're moving towards more  free speech we're allowing more free  speech I think we're already seeing the  limits of what his own personal  definition of what that looks like is on  the platform  what's clear now is that Twitter is Elon  musk's own private platform where only  he decides who is allowed to tweet and  who gets suspended if they cross him  Gabriel lozondo Al Jazeera New York
 

